"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[35970],{35970:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n## uiautomator dump\\n```uiautomator``` is a UI testing framework provided by Android.  \\nThe important thing is that system-level manipulation is possible.  \\n\\n\\nYou can manipulate not only the app you created but also other apps appearing on the screen.  \\nTherefore, it is essential for testing interactions or automation.  \\n\\n\\nYou can see the <mark>hierarchy of all UI elements</mark> visible on the current screen in XML format.\\n```sh\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"uiautomator dump\\"\\n}\\n---\\n$ adb shell uiautomator dump /sdcard/window_dump.xml\\n$ adb pull /sdcard/window_dump.xml\\n```\\nAn example of the dump XML is shown below.\\n```xml\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"UI Hierarchy example\\"\\n}\\n---\\n<hierarchy rotation=\\"0\\">\\n  <node index=\\"0\\" text=\\"\\" resource-id=\\"\\" class=\\"android.widget.FrameLayout\\" package=\\"com.android.systemui\\" ...>\\n    <node index=\\"0\\" text=\\"12:00\\" resource-id=\\"com.android.systemui:id/clock\\" class=\\"android.widget.TextView\\" bounds=\\"[50,20][200,80]\\" ... />\\n    <node index=\\"1\\" text=\\"OK\\" resource-id=\\"android:id/button1\\" class=\\"android.widget.Button\\" bounds=\\"[100,1000][300,1100]\\" clickable=\\"true\\" ... />\\n  </node>\\n</hierarchy>\\n```"}')}}]);